# __PROJECT_NAME__

__DESCRIPTION__

An Electron + Vite + React 19 desktop app. Standard electron-vite layout;
all logic lives in the UI-free `src/main/core/` boundary.

## Install

```bash
npm install          # postinstall: rebuild natives for Electron
npm run rebuild:node # rebuild for Node before running tests
```

## Develop

```bash
npm run dev          # electron-vite dev
```

Editing `src/main/**` rebuilds and restarts the main process. Editing
`src/renderer/**` hot-reloads.

## Test and check

```bash
npm test             # vitest
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
```

## Package

```bash
npm run rebuild      # Electron-ABI native modules
npm run dist:mac     # or dist:win / dist:linux
```

Installers land in `release/`.

## Layout

```
src/main/             Electron main process entry.
  index.ts            Window lifecycle; calls configureAppHome(userData).
  ipc.ts              Thin IPC handlers, one ipcMain.handle per channel.
  core/               UI-free logic. Knows nothing about Electron or React.
    index.ts          The public surface. The shell imports only from here.
    events.ts         Event vocabulary that crosses the core → UI boundary.
    bus.ts            JobEventBus — the only channel out of core.
    jobs/             Long-running work. Takes emit + AbortSignal.
    store/            SQLite (better-sqlite3): db, schema, runs.
src/preload/          contextBridge surface. Type imports of core only.
src/renderer/         React 19 UI (index.html + src/).
tests/                Job behaviour, boundary guard, surface canary, IPC contract.
scripts/              Native module rebuild for Electron / for Node.
```

State lives in the app's `userData` dir (macOS:
`~/Library/Application Support/__PROJECT_NAME__/`). Set `__ENV_PREFIX___HOME`
to move it, or `__ENV_PREFIX___TEST_DB` to point the SQLite file elsewhere in
tests.
